"id": "roles-law",
"sec": "01 · Role & responsibilities",
"html": "<section id=\"roles-law\">\n<p class=\"eyebrow\">The law and the workplace</p>\n<h2>First aid at work</h2>\n<table class=\"tbl\"><tr><th style=\"width:30%\">Topic</th><th style=\"width:70%\">What you need to know</th></tr><tr><td>The law</td><td>Health and Safety (First-Aid) Regulations 1981</td></tr><tr><td>How much cover</td><td>The employer decides through a first aid needs assessment</td></tr><tr><td>Appointed person</td><td>Looks after first aid arrangements and calls the emergency services</td></tr><tr><td>First aid kit</td><td>Dressings, bandages, gloves. No tablets or medicines</td></tr><tr><td>Certificate</td><td>Valid for 3 years, plus a recommended annual refresher</td></tr><tr><td>Emergency numbers</td><td>999 or 112 (111 is the NHS non-emergency line)</td></tr></table>\n<div class=\"foot\"><p>EFAW · Role &amp; responsibilities</p><p class=\"pg\">6</p></div>\n</section>",
"notes": "Check that learners know where their own workplace first aid kit and accident book are kept.",
